---
description: StateRoot persistent project state protocol — resume, checkpoint, handoff
globs:
alwaysApply: true
---

This project uses StateRoot for persistent, harness-neutral project state (`.stateroot/`).

1. At session start, prefer the auto-injected StateRoot digest from hooks when present. Only run `stateroot resume --harness cursor` if no digest appeared yet. Do not run resume twice unless the user asks (`--force` reprints).
2. After every step that changes project state — files written, decisions made, milestones, blockers — run `stateroot checkpoint --note "<what changed and why>"`.
3. Before attempting a non-trivial approach, check the failed-approaches log with `stateroot search "failed approach <topic>"` and do not repeat recorded failures.
4. Before ending a session, when approaching usage limits, or when asked to switch harness, write strict structured JSON and run `stateroot handoff write --from cursor --to <harness> --input <handoff.json>`. Include durable objective, immediate task, a detailed continuity narrative in `context_summary`, decisions with rationale, truthful failures, and next actions; verified recent conversation is auto-captured. Do not paste giant dumps into legacy `--note`. Normal Windows paths work; `--input -` is optional stdin convenience.
5. Never edit files under `.stateroot/` directly; all state access goes through the `stateroot` CLI. The CLI is offline-safe and queues operations locally when the network is down.
